Author or edit a Hive Desktop agent workspace: a named, durable directory
where a CLI agent runs against a purpose-built MCP tool set, for work that has
no repository.
{{template "app" .}}
Every workspace lives under {{.Env.AgentWorkspacesDir}}:

    {{.Env.AgentWorkspacesDir}}/mcps.yaml                     — your own MCP server library
    {{.Env.AgentWorkspacesDir}}/.shared/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md — merged into every workspace
    {{.Env.AgentWorkspacesDir}}/<dir>/agent-workspace.yaml     — one workspace's manifest
    {{.Env.AgentWorkspacesDir}}/<dir>/AGENTS.md                — the workspace's own instructions, hand-edited

`<dir>` is the workspace's directory name and its whole identity — there is no
separate id field, so create one by creating the directory. Opening a
workspace regenerates everything else under `<dir>` (`CLAUDE.md`, `.mcp.json`,
`.codex/config.toml`, `.claude/`, `.agents/`, an empty `docs/`) from the
manifest and `AGENTS.md`. None of that generated output is meant to be
hand-edited — it is silently replaced the next time the workspace opens. Put
prose in `AGENTS.md`, not in the manifest: `agent-workspace.yaml` carries no
`system_prompt` field.
{{template "yaml-strict" .}}
## agent-workspace.yaml schema

- `version` — must be `1`.
- `name` — display name shown on the workspace's card.
- `agent` — which CLI agent runs sessions here. Hive currently knows `claude` and `codex`.
- `autonomy` — one of `ask`, `auto`, or `full`; omitted defaults to `ask`. `ask` leaves every prompt to the agent CLI's own defaults, and is what the area's approval indicator shows you waiting on; `auto` accepts edits but still asks about anything riskier; `full` skips prompting entirely — reserve it for a workspace you already trust completely.
- `mcps` — optional list of MCP server ids this workspace enables. Each id is either one of the shipped catalogue entries below or a key from your own mcps.yaml `servers:` map; an mcps.yaml entry can also replace a shipped entry of the same id.
- `skills` — optional list of installed skill slugs to render into this workspace's `.claude/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`, on top of whatever `.shared/skills/` already merges in. Slugs carry the installed `hive-` prefix (`hive-http-api`, not `http-api`) — the same names `.shared/skills/<slug>/` directories use. A slug declared here wins over a `.shared/` skill of the same name.

## mcps.yaml schema

Your own MCP server library — the escape hatch beyond the shipped catalogue.

- `version` — must be `1`.
- `servers` — a map of id to server declaration. Each entry is one of:
  - a **stdio** server: `command` (required), `args`, `env`.
  - an **http** or **sse** server: `type: http` or `type: sse`, `url` (required), `headers`.

  `type` defaults to `stdio` when omitted. A stdio entry rejects `url`/`headers`; an http or sse entry rejects `command`/`args`/`env`.

